-- Renames keys that earlier hand-written migrations let PostgreSQL name, so the database
-- uses the names in the Drizzle snapshot. drizzle-kit writes later migrations from the
-- snapshot, and a statement naming a key the database calls something else would fail.
-- Only names change: no key is added, dropped or checked again and no row is read or
-- written. A renamed unique constraint or primary key renames its index too. PostgreSQL
-- keeps the first 63 bytes of a longer name, as it does in generated migrations.
-- Created by 0007_operational_publication
